<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="generator" content="ullage {{.Version}}">
<meta name="robots" content="noindex">
<title>ullage — unused accelerator capacity{{if .Context}} — {{.Context}}{{end}}</title>
<style>{{.CSS}}</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

<header class="masthead">
  <h1 class="wordmark">ullage <span class="tag">— the GPU your cluster paid for and didn't use</span></h1>
  <ul class="meta">
    {{if .Context}}<li>cluster <code>{{.Context}}</code></li>{{end}}
    <li>window <code>{{.WindowLabel}}</code></li>
    <li>scanned <code>{{.Started}}</code></li>
    <li>ullage <code>{{.Version}}</code></li>
    {{if .Prometheus}}<li>metrics <code>{{.Prometheus}}</code></li>{{end}}
  </ul>
  <p class="assurance">
    <span>read-only scan</span>
    <span>offline document</span>
    <span>no telemetry</span>
    {{if .Redacted}}<span>redacted</span>{{end}}
  </p>
</header>

<!-- Headline -->
{{if .Findings}}
<div class="headline">
  <div class="big">{{.Headline}} accelerator-hours unused</div>
  <div class="qualifier">
    {{.HeadlineSub}} — {{.UnusedPct}}% of the bill.
    {{if .HasCost}}Worth <strong>{{.Cost}}</strong> at the rates below.{{end}}
  </div>
</div>
{{else}}
<div class="headline">
  <div class="nothing">Nothing to reclaim.</div>
  <div class="qualifier">
    No accelerator in this cluster held capacity without using it for the whole
    {{.WindowLabel}} window. {{.HeadlineSub}}.
  </div>
</div>
{{end}}

{{if not .Ledger.Reconciles}}
<div class="notice" role="alert">
  <h3>Capacity reconciliation unavailable</h3>
  <p>
    The buckets below do not sum to the capacity paid for
    ({{printf "%.1f" .Ledger.Discrepancy}} accelerator-hours out). Findings may
    describe the same devices twice, so no proportional chart is drawn. The
    individual findings are still shown, and the JSON output carries the
    underlying numbers.
  </p>
</div>
{{end}}

<!-- Where the capacity went -->
<section id="capacity">
  <h2>Where the capacity went</h2>
  <div class="panel">
    <p class="lede">
      Every accelerator-hour the cluster paid for during the window, sorted into
      one bucket each. ullage removes what it cannot judge and what is empty on
      purpose <em>before</em> it calls anything waste.
    </p>

    {{if .Ledger.Reconciles}}
    <svg class="waterfall" viewBox="0 0 720 74" role="img"
         aria-labelledby="capTitle capDesc" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet">
      <title id="capTitle">Paid accelerator-hours by bucket</title>
      <desc id="capDesc">
        {{hours .Ledger.Paid}} accelerator-hours paid for in total.
        {{range .Ledger.Rows}}{{hours .Hours}} {{.Label}}. {{end}}
        The same figures appear in the table immediately below.
      </desc>
      <defs>
        <pattern id="hatch" width="7" height="7" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"
                 patternTransform="rotate(45)">
          <rect width="7" height="7" fill="var(--design-soft)"/>
          <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="7" stroke="var(--design)" stroke-width="3"/>
        </pattern>
      </defs>
      <rect class="track" x="0" y="8" width="720" height="34" rx="4"/>
      {{$x := 0.0}}
      {{range .Ledger.Rows}}
        {{if gt .Hours 0.0}}
        <rect class="{{rowClass .Key}}" x="{{printf "%.2f" $x}}" y="8"
              width="{{printf "%.2f" .Width}}" height="34">
          <title>{{.Label}} — {{hours .Hours}} accelerator-hours</title>
        </rect>
        {{$x = .Next}}
        {{end}}
      {{end}}
      <rect x="0" y="8" width="720" height="34" rx="4" fill="none"
            stroke="var(--rule)" stroke-width="1"/>
      <text class="sub" x="0" y="60">0</text>
      <text class="sub" x="720" y="60" text-anchor="end">{{hours .Ledger.Paid}} accelerator-hours paid</text>
    </svg>
    {{end}}

    <table>
      <caption class="visually-hidden">Paid accelerator-hours by bucket</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Bucket</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">Accelerators</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">Hours</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">Share</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {{range .Ledger.Rows}}
        <tr>
          <td>
            <span class="swatch {{swatch .Key}}" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{.Label}}
            <span class="rownote">{{.Note}}</span>
          </td>
          <td class="num">{{if gt .Accelerators 0}}{{.Accelerators}}{{else}}—{{end}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{hours .Hours}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{.SharePct}}</td>
        </tr>
        {{end}}
        <tr class="total">
          <td>Paid capacity</td>
          <td class="num">{{.Observed}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{hours .Ledger.Paid}}</td>
          <td class="num">100%</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p class="footnote">
      &ldquo;Unflagged&rdquo; is a remainder, not a
      measurement: ullage counts unused hours, not productive ones, so an hour
      in that row may be real work or may be idleness too short to report.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- How this was measured -->
<section id="method">
  <h2>How this was measured</h2>
  <div class="panel">
    <p class="lede">
      Every figure above came from four steps, and each one was allowed to
      answer <em>“I don’t know”</em>.
    </p>

    <ol class="method">
      <li>
        <strong>Count what is there.</strong> Nodes and pods were read from the
        Kubernetes API. A device is judged only where one pod exclusively holds
        one physical accelerator — the only case in which “the device was idle”
        and “this workload was idle” mean the same thing. Shared and partitioned
        devices are counted, then set aside.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Ask whether it did any work.</strong> Not one gauge — every
        signal below. A device where <em>any</em> of them was ever non-zero is
        not idle.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Measure how long it has been quiet.</strong> Unused time is the
        unbroken run of zeros up to now, not an average. Capacity is charged per
        node for <code>min(node age, window) × accelerators</code>, so a node
        created this morning is not billed for the whole window.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Find who can act.</strong> Ownership resolves pod → controller →
        namespace. Each finding shows the label it was resolved from, so a wrong
        answer is correctable rather than just annoying.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <table>
      <caption class="visually-hidden">Signals consulted when deciding a device did no work</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Signal</th>
          <th scope="col">What it catches</th>
          <th scope="col">In this scan</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {{range .Signals}}
        <tr>
          <td><code>{{.Metric}}</code></td>
          <td>{{.Answers}}</td>
          <td>{{if .Consulted}}<span class="yes">checked</span>{{else}}<span class="no">not available</span>{{end}}</td>
        </tr>
        {{end}}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="footnote">
      SM utilization alone would have reported a video pipeline, a data loader,
      or a warm model parked in framebuffer as doing nothing at all. Any signal
      marked unavailable is a blind spot in the findings below, not an absence
      of work.
    </p>

    <h3>When no claim is made</h3>
    <ul class="rules">
      <li><strong>Absent samples are not zero samples.</strong> A series that
        returned nothing is unknown. Otherwise an exporter that died last week
        would look like a fleet that stopped working.</li>
      <li><strong>Disagreement wins.</strong> The aggregate and the stepped range
        query are asked separately. When the aggregate proves work happened but
        the range query cannot say when, nothing is reported.</li>
      <li><strong>Thin evidence withdraws or caps the claim.</strong> Below 80%
        sample coverage no finding is produced; below 95%, or with no power
        series to corroborate, it is capped at medium confidence.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="footnote">
      Thresholds in force: idle ≥ {{.IdleLabel}}, stuck ≥
      {{.StuckLabel}}, sampled every {{.StepLabel}}, showing
      {{.MinConfidence}} confidence and above. Run
      <code>ullage --explain-queries</code> for the exact PromQL.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Evidence quality -->
{{if or .Exclusions .Warnings .HasCovers .UnmetDemand}}
<section id="evidence">
  <h2>What this scan could not see</h2>
  <div class="panel">
    {{if .HasCovers}}
    <p class="lede">
      The sparsest series behind a finding covered <strong>{{.Coverage}}</strong>
      of the samples the window should have contained. Missing samples are never
      read as zeroes: a dead exporter and an idle fleet look identical, so
      confidence drops instead.
    </p>
    {{end}}

    {{if .Exclusions}}
    <table>
      <caption class="visually-hidden">Accelerators excluded from analysis</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Code</th>
          <th scope="col">Excluded</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">Accelerators</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {{range .Exclusions}}
        <tr>
          <td><code>{{.Code}}</code></td>
          <td>{{.Detail}}{{if .Remedy}}<span class="rownote">{{.Remedy}}</span>{{end}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{.Accelerators}}</td>
        </tr>
        {{end}}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    {{end}}

    {{if .UnmetDemand}}
    <p class="footnote">
      <strong>{{.UnmetDemand.Accelerators}} accelerators are being waited on.</strong>
      {{.UnmetDemand.Detail}}. Capacity released here has somewhere to go.
    </p>
    {{end}}

    {{range .Warnings}}<p class="footnote">⚠ {{.}}</p>{{end}}
  </div>
</section>
{{end}}

<!-- Reserved on purpose -->
{{if .ByDesign}}
<section id="by-design">
  <h2>Reserved on purpose</h2>
  <div class="panel">
    <p class="lede">
      Capacity held idle deliberately — an autoscaler floor, a reservation, a
      warm pool. It is listed so the decision stays visible, and it is excluded
      from every total above. It is not waste.
    </p>
    {{range .ByDesign}}
    <details class="finding">
      <summary>
        <span class="rank" aria-hidden="true">—</span>
        <span>
          <span class="subject">{{.Subject}}<span class="kindtag">{{.Kind}}</span></span>
          <span class="subject-sub">{{.SubjectSub}}</span>
          <span class="badges">
            <span class="badge design">reserved by policy</span>
            <span class="badge">excluded from waste</span>
          </span>
        </span>
        <span class="figures">
          {{if .HasCost}}<span class="cost">{{.Cost}}</span>{{end}}
          <span class="hrs">{{.Hours}} acc-h</span>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <div class="body">
        {{if .Because}}<p class="claim">{{.Because}}</p>{{end}}
        <dl class="kv">
          <dt>Accelerators</dt><dd>{{.Accelerators}}</dd>
          <dt>Idle for</dt><dd>{{.Unused}} of {{.Window}}</dd>
          {{if .Owner}}<dt>Owner</dt><dd>{{.Owner}}{{if .OwnerVia}} <span class="rownote">via {{.OwnerVia}}</span>{{end}}</dd>{{end}}
        </dl>
      </div>
    </details>
    {{end}}
  </div>
</section>
{{end}}

<!-- Owners -->
{{if .Owners}}
<section id="owners">
  <h2>Who is holding it</h2>
  <div class="panel">
    <p class="lede">
      Unused accelerator-hours grouped by the owner ullage resolved, ranked by
      {{.OwnerMeasure}}. This ranks opportunities, not people: the largest bar
      is usually the easiest conversation, not the worst offender.
    </p>
    <ul class="owners">
      {{range .Owners}}
      <li>
        <div class="owner-head">
          <span class="owner-name">{{.Name}}</span>
          <span class="owner-fig">
            {{.Hours}} acc-h{{if .HasCost}} · {{.Cost}}{{end}} · {{.Count}} finding{{if ne .Count 1}}s{{end}}
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="owner-track">
          <div class="owner-fill" style="width:{{pct .Share}}"></div>
        </div>
      </li>
      {{end}}
    </ul>
    {{if .OwnersOmitted}}
    <p class="footnote">
      {{.OwnersOmitted}} further owner{{if ne .OwnersOmitted 1}}s{{end}} not
      charted. Every one of them appears in the findings below.
    </p>
    {{end}}
  </div>
</section>
{{end}}

<!-- Findings -->
{{if .Findings}}
<section id="findings">
  <h2>Findings</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    Ranked by what they cost, not by how idle they look. Open one for the
    evidence behind the claim, what it deliberately stops short of saying, and
    the command that frees the capacity.
  </p>
  {{range .Findings}}
  <details class="finding" id="{{.Anchor}}">
    <summary>
      <span class="rank">{{.Rank}}</span>
      <span>
        <span class="subject">{{.Subject}}<span class="kindtag">{{.Kind}}</span></span>
        <span class="subject-sub">{{.SubjectSub}}</span>
        <span class="badges">
          <span class="badge">{{.CheckLabel}}</span>
          <span class="badge {{.ConfClass}}">{{.Confidence}} confidence</span>
          {{if .Owner}}<span class="badge">{{.Owner}}</span>{{end}}
          {{if not .Command}}<span class="badge">no safe command</span>{{end}}
        </span>
      </span>
      <span class="figures">
        {{if .HasCost}}<span class="cost">{{.Cost}}</span>{{end}}
        <span class="hrs">{{.Hours}} acc-h</span>
      </span>
    </summary>

    <div class="body">
      <dl class="kv">
        <dt>Accelerators</dt><dd>{{.Accelerators}}</dd>
        <dt>Idle for</dt><dd>{{.Unused}} of a {{.Window}} window</dd>
        <dt>Last did work</dt><dd>{{.LastSeen}}</dd>
        <dt>Peak utilization</dt><dd>{{.UtilMax}} — the highest sample, not the mean</dd>
        {{if .Power}}<dt>Power draw</dt><dd>{{.Power}}</dd>{{end}}
        <dt>Sample coverage</dt><dd>{{.Completeness}}</dd>
        {{if .Owner}}<dt>Owner</dt><dd>{{.Owner}}{{if .OwnerVia}} <span class="rownote">resolved via {{.OwnerVia}}</span>{{end}}</dd>{{end}}
        <dt>Ownership</dt><dd>{{.Ownership}}</dd>
        {{if .Controller}}<dt>Controlled by</dt><dd><code>{{.Controller}}</code></dd>{{end}}
        {{if .ShowChain}}<dt>Owner chain</dt><dd>{{range $i, $c := .Chain}}{{if $i}} → {{end}}<code>{{$c}}</code>{{end}}</dd>{{end}}
      </dl>

      {{range .Notes}}<p class="claim">{{.}}</p>{{end}}

      {{if .Risk}}
      <p class="risk"><strong>Before you run this.</strong> {{.Risk}}</p>
      {{end}}

      {{if .Blockers}}
      <p class="cmd-label">What is holding it</p>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          {{range .Blockers}}
          <tr><td><code>{{.Object}}</code></td><td>{{.Reason}}</td></tr>
          {{end}}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      {{end}}

      {{if .Command}}
      <div class="cmd">
        <div class="cmd-label">
          Frees {{.Targets}}{{if .Frees}} — {{.Frees}}{{end}}
        </div>
        <div class="cmd-row">
          <pre class="cmd-text" id="{{.CommandID}}">{{.Command}}</pre>
          <button class="copy" type="button" data-for="{{.CommandID}}" hidden>copy</button>
        </div>
        {{if .Rationale}}<p class="footnote">{{.Rationale}}</p>{{end}}
      </div>
      {{else}}
      <p class="blocked">
        No command is offered here. {{if .Rationale}}{{.Rationale}}{{else}}ullage
        emits one only where it knows the removal semantics of the owning
        controller.{{end}}
      </p>
      {{end}}
    </div>
  </details>
  {{end}}
</section>
{{end}}

<!-- Suppressed -->
{{if .Suppressed}}
<section id="suppressed">
  <h2>Suppressed</h2>
  <div class="panel">
    <p class="lede">
      Silenced by <code>.ullage.yaml</code>, and still counted in the ledger
      above. A suppression hides a finding from the ranking, not the capacity
      from the bill.
    </p>
    <ul class="owners">
      {{range .Suppressed}}
      <li>
        <div class="owner-head">
          <span class="owner-name">{{.Subject}}</span>
          <span class="owner-fig">{{.Hours}} acc-h{{if .HasCost}} · {{.Cost}}{{end}}</span>
        </div>
        {{if .Because}}<span class="rownote">{{.Because}}</span>{{end}}
      </li>
      {{end}}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
{{end}}

<footer>
  <p><strong>How to read this.</strong>
    ullage measures accelerator-hours that were paid for and did no work. It does
    not measure efficiency, and a low utilization figure is not a finding here —
    only capacity that did nothing at all for longer than the threshold.</p>
  {{if .PricingSource}}
  <p><strong>Money.</strong> {{.PricingSource}}. Costs are estimates of what the
    unused capacity was billed at, not savings that will appear on an invoice;
    releasing capacity only saves money if the underlying node goes away.</p>
  {{end}}
  <p>Generated {{.Generated}} by ullage {{.Version}}. This document made no
    network request to render, and contains no tracking of any kind.</p>
</footer>

</div>
<script>{{.JS}}</script>
</body>
</html>
